## Version 4: Pruning Engine V2 Rewrite (Projection-Profile Approach)

### Phase 1: Background Detection (F1)
- [x] Estimate background color from image border pixels (mode of grayscale values)
- [x] Works for light themes (white/gray bg) AND dark themes (black/dark bg)
- [x] No hardcoded white assumption — detects any background color
- [x] Verified: white bg detected >200, dark bg detected <60

### Phase 2: Content Mask (F2)
- [x] Build content mask via abs-difference from estimated background
- [x] Configurable tolerance (BG_TOLERANCE=15, range 12-20)
- [x] Works for both light and dark themes
- [x] Verified: 100% content detection on synthetic light and dark images

### Phase 3: Projection Profiles (F3)
- [x] Compute row projection profile (content pixels per row)
- [x] Compute column projection profile (content pixels per column)
- [x] Used for whitespace detection instead of contour bounding boxes
- [x] Verified: correctly identifies empty/content rows and columns

### Phase 4: Whitespace Collapse (F4)
- [x] Find empty runs (consecutive rows/cols with zero content pixels)
- [x] Collapse runs longer than MIN_GAP (24px) down to GAP_KEEP (8px)
- [x] Preserve short gaps (<MIN_GAP) entirely — no content loss
- [x] Apply both horizontally and vertically
- [x] Verified: 200px test image collapses to 126px, all content preserved

### Phase 5: Coordinate Map (F5)
- [x] Return CoordinateMap alongside pruned image
- [x] Segment-based mapping: list of (pruned_start, original_start, length) per axis
- [x] Helper functions: pruned_to_original(x, y) and original_to_pruned(x, y)
- [x] Verified: round-trip error <=1px on 20 random content pixels

### Phase 6: Sample Capture (F6)
- [x] Capture 4 real screenshots via Playwright: wikipedia, amazon, github dark, dense text
- [x] Samples stored in samples/ directory
- [x] Verified: all 4 screenshots captured successfully

